  "reasoning": "The patient presents with a recurring burning pain in the stomach, along with gas and bloating, which are hallmark gastrointestinal symptoms. The accompanying weight loss and loss of appetite commonly occur in this condition as patients may avoid eating to prevent discomfort or due to altered digestion. Most critically, the presence of dark, tarry stools (melena) and blood in the vomit (hematemesis) are definitive clinical signs of upper gastrointestinal bleeding. This specific combination of burning epigastric pain and GI bleeding strongly aligns with peptic ulcer disease.",
  "final_answer": "[DIAGNOSIS]peptic ulcer disease[/DIAGNOSIS]"
